verses.commentary:
10:21 This phrase refers to the pagans' sacrifices and rituals in the pagan temples of Corinth. A believer
cannot affirm the exclusiveness of Christianity (i.e., one and only one true God and Jesus His Messiah, cf. John 14:6;
Acts 4:22; 1 Tim. 2:5) and still spiritually participate in pagan worship. If they do, it is spiritual adultery!
